### ADR-002: Backend & Database — Supabase (PostgreSQL)

**Status**: Accepted
**Date**: [YYYY-MM-DD]

#### Context
Need managed PostgreSQL with:
- Auth (email/password, OAuth, MFA)
- Real-time subscriptions
- Row Level Security (RLS)
- Edge-compatible (Cloudflare Workers)
- Generous free tier

#### Decision
Use **Supabase** as the primary backend platform (PostgreSQL + Auth + Realtime + Storage).

#### Consequences
**Positive**:
- PostgreSQL (not forked) — standard SQL, tooling, extensions
- Auth integrated with RLS — JWT claims map to policies
- Real-time via WebSockets (Postgres changes → clients)
- Edge-compatible client (`@supabase/supabase-js` works in Workers)
- Generous free tier (500MB DB, 50k MAU)
- Self-hostable exit strategy

**Negative**:
- Vendor lock-in on Auth/Realtime/Storage APIs
- Connection pooling required for serverless (PgBouncer)
- Cold starts on free tier
- Limited control over Postgres config (extensions, versions)

**Neutral**:
- Must design RLS policies carefully — security boundary

#### Alternatives Considered
| Alternative | Pros | Cons | Why Not Chosen |
|-------------|------|------|----------------|
| Neon + Clerk + Custom | Serverless Postgres, separate best-in-class auth | More moving parts, integration complexity | Supabase = integrated DX |
| PlanetScale + Kinde | MySQL-compatible, scalable | MySQL not PostgreSQL, different semantics | Team prefers Postgres |
| Railway/Render + Custom | Simpler, cheaper at scale | No built-in auth/realtime, more ops | Speed to market |
| Cloudflare D1 + Custom | Native Workers integration | SQLite limitations, no auth/realtime | Not production-ready for auth |

#### Implementation Notes
- Use Supabase JS client in Next.js Server Actions / Route Handlers (not browser)
- Enable RLS on all tables; policies reference `auth.uid()`
- Use `supabase.auth.getUser()` in server actions for session validation
- Connection pooling via Supavisor (built-in) — use `pooler.supabase.com:6543`
- Migrations via Supabase CLI (`supabase db push` / migration files)
- Storage buckets for user uploads; signed URLs for private files

#### Validation Criteria
- [ ] RLS policies block cross-tenant access in integration tests
- [ ] Auth flows work end-to-end (signup, login, MFA, password reset)
- [ ] Real-time subscriptions work in Cloudflare Pages preview
- [ ] PgBouncer connection pool handles 100 concurrent serverless invocations

