### ADR-007: API Layer — Next.js Server Actions + Route Handlers (RPC)

**Status**: Accepted
**Date**: [YYYY-MM-DD]

#### Context
Need type-safe API between frontend and backend without:
- REST/OpenAPI boilerplate
- GraphQL complexity
- Separate backend deployment

#### Decision
Use **Next.js Server Actions** (`"use server"`) as the primary mutation layer (RPC-style, co-located) + **Route Handlers** (`app/api/.../route.ts`) pour les endpoints externes (webhooks, API publique). Validation d'entrée avec **Zod** sur chaque action/route.

#### Consequences
**Positive**:
- End-to-end TypeScript types (inputs validated with Zod)
- RSC-native — pas de fetch client pour les mutations
- Middleware support (auth, rate limit, logging)
- No separate API gateway needed

**Negative**:
- Server Actions ne sont pas une API publique — consumers externes passent par Route Handlers
- Tests require mocking ou setup d'intégration
- Attention aux re-renders / progressive enhancement

**Neutral**:
- API publique (si nécessaire) buildée comme Route Handlers séparés

#### Implementation Notes
```typescript
// app/actions/get-user.ts
"use server";
import { z } from "zod";
import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/server";

const schema = z.object({ id: z.string().uuid() });

export async function getUser(input: unknown) {
  const { id } = schema.parse(input);
  const supabase = createClient();
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from("profiles").select("*").eq("id", id).single();
  if (error) throw error;
  return data;
}

// Route Handler : app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  // verify webhook signature, process event, return 200
}
```

#### Validation Criteria
- [ ] TypeScript catches input/output mismatches at compile time
- [ ] Server Actions + Route Handlers deploy to Cloudflare Pages
- [ ] Middleware runs on every call (auth, rate limit)
- [ ] Error serialization works (Zod errors → client)

